	// From earlier: "set -x -g 'NEWLINE' 'a'\\n'b';" - That's 'a' + \n + 'b' concatenated? In fish, 'a'\n'b' means 'a' + newline escape + 'b'?
	// Similarly for unicode: "'h'\\Xc3''\\Xa9'llo'"? Actually "'h'\\Xc3''\\Xa9'llo'" - That's 'h' + \Xc3 + '' + \Xa9 + 'llo'? Hmm.
